Compare two designs:

```java
// Design 1
class Car {
    private final Engine engine;
    Car() { this.engine = new Engine(); }
}

// Design 2
class Car {
    private Driver driver;
    void assignDriver(Driver driver) { this.driver = driver; }
}
```

In Design 1, the Engine is created inside Car's constructor and never exposed; in Design 2, a Driver object is created elsewhere and merely handed to Car through a setter-like method. Which statement correctly classifies these two has-a relationships?
